‎{
‎  "title": "CHAPTER 1 : INTRODUCING PHILOSOPHY",
‎  "content": "<b><font color='#2E7D32'>ሰላም ሰላም! ውድ የEthioFresh ቤተሰቦች፤ እንኳን ወደ Logic & Critical Thinking Chapter 1, Lesson 4 በሰላም መጣችሁ! ዛሬ የፊሎሶፊን ሁለት በጣም አስደሳችና መሠረታዊ ዘርፎች (Axiology እና Logic) በጥልቀት እንመረምራለን። ዝግጁ ከሆናችሁ ፈገግ ብላችሁ ወደ ትምህርቱ እንለፍ! 😄👇👇👇</font></b><br><br><hr><br><b><font color='#1565C0'>Lesson 4: Axiology and Logic</font></b><br><br><b>Lesson Overview ፡</b><br>• Axiology is the philosophical study of value, which originally meant the worth of something. It includes the studies of moral values, aesthetic values, as well as political and social values.<br>👉 አክሲዮሎጂ (Axiological study) ማለት ስለ እሴት/ዋጋ (Value/Worth) የሚያጠና የፊሎሶፊ ዘርፍ ነው። የሞራል እሴቶች፣ የስነ-ውበት (Aesthetics) እሴቶች፣ እንዲሁም የማህበራዊና ፖለቲካዊ እሴቶችን ያጠናል።<br>• Logic, on the other hand, is a philosophical study of arguments and the methods and principles of right reasoning. In this lesson, we will discuss Axiology and Logic as the other two major fields of philosophy.<br>👉 ሎጂክ ደግሞ ትክክለኛ የሞገት (Argument) እና የአስተሳሰብ መርሆዎችንና ዘዴዎችን የሚያጠና የፊሎሶፊ ዋና ዘርፍ ነው።<br><br><b>Lesson Objectives / የትምህርቱ ዓላማዎች፡</b><br>• Understand the fundamental concern and issues that axiology and logic primarily deal with.<br>👉 አክሲዮሎጂ እና ሎጂክ የሚያተኩሩባቸውን መሠረታዊ ጉዳዮች መረዳት።<br>• Identify the major subsets or aspects of axiological questions: ethical, aesthetical, political and social questions.<br>👉 የአክሲዮሎጂ ዋና ዋና ክፍሎችን (ኤቲክስ፣ ኤስቴቲክስ፣ ሶሻል/ፖሊቲካል) መለየት።<br>• Recognize the fundamental philosophical debates concerning the nature and sources of moral, political and social rules and principles.<br>👉 በሞራል፣ ፖለቲካዊ እና ማህበራዊ ህጎች መነሻ ላይ ያሉ የፊሎሶፊ ክርክሮችን መገንዘብ።<br><br><hr><br><b><font color='#1565C0'>4.1 Axiology (ስለ እሴቶችና ዋጋ የሚያጠና ዘርፍ)</font></b><br><br><b>Definition & Etymology ፡</b><br>• Axiology stems from two Greek words: <i>\"Axios\"</i> (meaning \"value, worth\") and <i>\"logos\"</i> (meaning \"reason/ theory/ symbol/ science/ study of\"). Hence, Axiology is the philosophical study of value, which originally meant the worth of something.<br>👉 አክሲዮሎጂ የሚለው ቃል \"Axios\" (እሴት/ዋጋ) እና \"Logos\" (ጥናት/ሳይንስ) ከሚሉ ሁለት የግሪክ ቃላት የተገኘ ሲሆን፣ ትርጉሙም ስለ እሴትና ዋጋ የሚያጠና የፊሎሶፊ ዘርፍ ማለት ነው።<br>• Axiology asks the philosophical questions of values that deal with notions of what a person or a society regards as good or preferable:<br>👉 አንድ ሰው ወይም ማህበረሰብ ጥሩ ወይም ተመራጭ ነው ብሎ ስለሚቀበላቸው እሴቶች የሚከተሉትን ጥያቄዎች ይጠይቃል፦<br>  - <i>What is a value?</i> (እሴት/ዋጋ ማለት ምንድን ነው?)<br>  - <i>Where do values come from?</i> (እሴቶች ከወዴት ይመጣሉ?)<br>  - <i>How do we justify our values? How do we know what is valuable?</i> (እሴቶቻችንን እንዴት እናረጋግጣለን? ጠቃሚ የሆነውን ነገርስ እንዴት እናውቃለን?)<br>  - <i>What is the relationship between values and knowledge?</i> (በእሴትና በእውቀት መካከል ያለው ግንኙነት ምንድን ነው?)<br>  - <i>What kinds of values exist? Can it be demonstrated that one value is better than another?</i> (ምን ዓይነት እሴቶች አሉ? አንዱ እሴት ከሌላው ይበልጣል ብሎ ማረጋገጥ ይቻላል?)<br>  - <i>Who benefits from values?</i> (ከእሴቶች ማን ይጠቀማል?)<br><br>• Axiology deals with issues of value in three areas: <b>Ethics</b>, <b>Aesthetics</b>, and <b>Social/Political Philosophy</b>.<br>👉 አክሲዮሎጂ በሦስት ዋና ዋና ዘርፎች ይከፈላል፦ ኤቲክስ፣ ኤስቴቲክስ እና ማህበራዊ/ፖለቲካዊ ፊሎሶፊ።<br><br><hr><br><b><font color='#00796B'>I. Ethics (Moral Philosophy / የሞራል ፊሎሶፊ)</font></b><br><br><b>Definition ፡</b><br>• Ethics (Moral Philosophy) is a science that deals with the philosophical study of moral principles, values, codes, and rules used as standards for determining what kind of human conduct/action is said to be good or bad, right or wrong.<br>👉 ኤቲክስ (የስነ-ምግባር ፊሎሶፊ) የሰውን ልጅ ድርጊት ጥሩ ወይም መጥፎ፣ ትክክል ወይም ስህተት ለማለት እንደ መስፈርት የሚያገለግሉ የሞራል መርሆችን፣ ህጎችንና እሴቶችን የሚያጠና ዘርፍ ነው።<br><br><b>Core Questions Ethics Raises / የኤቲክስ ዋና ጥያቄዎች፡</b><br>• What is good/bad? What is right/wrong?<br>👉 ጥሩ/መጥፎ ወይም ትክክል/ስህተት የሚባለው ምንድን ነው?<br>• Is it the Right Principle or the Good End that makes human action/conduct moral? Is an action right because of its good end, or is it good because of its right principle?<br>👉 የአንድን ሰው ድርጊት የሞራል ግዴታ የሚያደርገው ትክክለኛው መርህ (Principle) ነው ወይስ የሚገኘው ጥሩ ውጤት (Good End)?<br>• Are moral principles universal, objective, and unconditional, or relative, subjective and conditional?<br>👉 የሞራል ህጎች ሁለንተናዊና የማይለወጡ (Universal/Objective) ናቸው ወይስ አንፃራዊና እንደ ሁኔታው የሚቀያየሩ (Relative/Subjective)?<br>• What is the ultimate foundation of moral principles? The supernatural God? Human reason? Mutual social contract? Social custom?<br>👉 የሞራል መርሆች መሠረት ምንድን ነው? ፈጣሪ፣ የሰው ልጅ አእምሮ፣ የማህበረሰብ ውል ወይስ ባህል?<br>• Does God exist? If so, is He Benevolent and Omnipotent? If God is Benevolent, why does He create evil things?<br>👉 ፈጣሪ አለ? ካለስ አምላክ ቸርና ሁሉን ቻይ ከሆነ በዓለም ላይ ክፉ ነገር ለምን በዛ?<br><br><b>Three Broad Categories of Ethics / የኤቲክስ ሦስቱ ዋና ክፍሎች፡</b><br><br><b>1. Normative Ethics :</b><br>• Attempts to study and determine precisely the moral rules, principles, standards, and goals by which human beings might evaluate and judge the moral values of their conducts. It is the reasoned search for principles of human conduct.<br>👉 የሰውን ልጅ ድርጊት \"ትክክል ነው\" ወይም \"ስህተት ነው\" ብለን እንድንፈርጅ የሚያስችሉ የሞራል ደንቦችንና መስፈርቶችን ያስቀምጣል።<br>• <b>Examples:</b> Consequentialism/Teleological Ethics (ውጤት ላይ የሚያተኩር)፣ Deontological Ethics (ግዴታና መርህ ላይ የሚያተኩር)፣ and Virtue Ethics (የስነ-ምግባር ሰብእና ላይ የሚያተኩር)።<br><br><b>2. Meta-ethics (መታ-ኤቲክስ):</b><br>• A highly technical philosophical discipline that deals with the investigation of the meaning of ethical terms, including a critical study of how ethical statements can be verified. It is concerned with the meanings of terms like <i>good</i>, <i>bad</i>, <i>right</i>, or <i>wrong</i>.<br>👉 ድርጊቱ ጥሩ ነው ወይስ መጥፎ ከሚለው ይልቅ \"ጥሩ\" (Good) ወይም \"ትክክል\" (Right) የሚሉ የኤቲክስ ቃላት አጠቃላይ ትርጉማቸውና አመጣጣቸው ምንድን ነው? በሚለው የቴክኒክ ጽንሰ-ሐሳብ ላይ ያተኩራል።<br>• <b>Examples:</b> Moral Intuitionism, Moral Emotivism, Moral Prescriptivism, Moral Nihilism, and Ethical Relativism.<br><br><b>3. Applied Ethics (ተግባራዊ ኤቲክስ):</b><br>• Attempts to explain, justify, and apply moral rules and principles to specific, real-world moral problems.<br>👉 አጠቃላይ የሞራል ህጎችን ወስዶ በተወሰኑ የዕለት ተዕለት ችግሮች ላይ ተግባራዊ ማድረግ ነው።<br>• <b>Examples:</b> Capital punishment (የሞት ቅጣት)፣ Euthanasia (በበሽታ ለሚሰቃይ ሰው በምህረት ህይወቱን ማለፍ)፣ Abortion (ፅንስ ማቋረጥ)፣ Adultery፣ Animal rights።<br><br><hr><br><b><font color='#00796B'>II. Aesthetics (የስነ-ውበት ፊሎሶፊ)</font></b><br><br><b>Definition ፡</b><br>• Aesthetics is the theory beauty. It studies about the particular value of our artistic and aesthetic experiences. It deals with beauty, art, enjoyment, sensory/emotional values, perception, and matters of taste and sentiment.<br>👉 ኤስቴቲክስ የስነ-ውበት ፊሎሶፊ ሲሆን ስለ ውበት፣ ጥበብ (Art)፣ የስሜት እርካታ እና ጣዕም የሚያጠና ዘርፍ ነው።<br><br><b>Typical Aesthetic Questions / የኤስቴቲክስ ጥያቄዎች፡</b><br>• <i>What is art? What is beauty? What is the relation between art and beauty?</i><br>👉 ጥበብ ምንድን ነው? ውበትስ ምንድን ነው? በሁለቱ መካከል ያለው ግንኙነትስ?<br>• <i>Can there be any objective standard by which we may judge the beauty of artistic works, or beauty is subjective?</i><br>👉 የጥበብ ሥራዎችን ውበት ለመመዘን የሚያስችል ወጥ የሆነ መስፈርት (Objective Standard) አለ ወይስ ውበት በግል እይታ የሚወሰን (Subjective) ነው?<br>• <i>What is artistic creativity and how does it differ from scientific creativity?</i><br>👉 የጥበብ ፈጠራ ከሳይንሳዊ ፈጠራ በምን ይለያል?<br>• <i>Does art have any moral value, obligations or constraints?</i><br>👉 ጥበብ የሞራል ግዴታ ወይም ወሰን አለበት?<br><br><hr><br><b><font color='#00796B'>III. Social/Political Philosophy (ማህበራዊ እና ፖለቲካዊ ፊሎሶፊ)</font></b><br><br><b>Definition ፡</b><br>• Social/Political Philosophy studies about the value judgments operating in a civil society, be it social or political.<br>👉 በማህበረሰብ ወይም በፖለቲካዊ መዋቅር ውስጥ ያሉ የእሴት ብይኖችን (Value Judgments) የሚያጠና የፊሎሶፊ ዘርፍ ነው።<br><br><b>Core Questions Raised ፡</b><br>• <i>What form of government is best? What economic system is best?</i><br>👉 የትኛው የመንግሥት ዓይነት ወይም የኢኮኖሚ ሥርዓት ለሕዝብ የተሻለ ነው?<br>• <i>What is justice/injustice? What makes an action/judgment just/unjust?</i><br>👉 ፍትህ (Justice) ማለት ምንድን ነው? አንድን ብይን ፍትሃዊ የሚያደርገው ምንድን ነው?<br>• <i>Are we obligated to obey all laws of the State? What is the purpose of government?</i><br>👉 የመንግሥትን ህጎች ሁሉ የመታዘዝ ግዴታ አለብን? የመንግሥት ዋና ዓላማስ ምንድን ነው?<br><br><div style='display: flex; flex-direction: column; width: 100%; max-width: 500px; margin: 10px 0; border: 1px solid #1565C0; border-radius: 6px; overflow: hidden;'><div style='display: flex; background-color: #1565C0; color: white; font-weight: bold; padding: 8px;'><div style='flex: 1;'>Branch</div><div style='flex: 1;'>Focus Area<div style='flex: 1;'</div><div style='display: flex; border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 8px;'><div style='flex: 1;'><b>Ethics</b></div><div style='flex: 1;'>Morality & Conduct</div><div style='flex: 1;'>ጥሩና መጥፎ ድርጊቶች</div></div><div style='display: flex; border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 8px; background-color: #f9f9f9;'><div style='flex: 1;'><b>Aesthetics</b></div><div style='flex: 1;'>Beauty & Art</div><div style='flex: 1;'>ስነ-ውበትና የጥበብ ስራዎች</div></div><div style='display: flex; padding: 8px;'><div style='flex: 1;'><b>Social/Political</b></div><div style='flex: 1;'>Society & Governance</div><div style='flex: 1;'>ፍትህ፣ መንግስትና ህግ</div></div></div><br><hr><br><b><font color='#1565C0'>4.2 Logic (ስለ ትክክለኛ አስተሳሰብና ሞገት የሚያጠና ዘርፍ)</font></b><br><br><b>Definition ፡</b><br>• Logic is the study or theory of principles of right reasoning. It deals with formulating the right principles of reasoning and developing scientific methods of evaluating the validity and soundness of arguments.<br>👉 ሎጂክ ማለት የትክክለኛ አስተሳሰብ/ምክንያት (Right reasoning) መርሆዎችን የሚያጠና ነው። የሞገቶችን (Arguments) ትክክለኛነት (Validity) እና አሳማኝነት (Soundness) የምንመዝንበትን ሳይንሳዊ መንገድ ያዘጋጃል።<br><br><b>Questions Raised by Logic / የሎጂክ ዋና ጥያቄዎች፡</b><br>• <i>What is an argument? What does it mean to argue?</i><br>👉 ሞገት (Argument) ማለት ምንድን ነው? መሞገትስ ማለት ምን ማለት ነው?<br>• <i>What makes an argument valid or invalid? What is a sound argument?</i><br>👉 አንድን ሞገት ትክክለኛ (Valid) የሚያደርገው ምንድን ነው? አሳማኝ ሞገትስ (Sound argument) ምንድን ነው?<br>• <i>What relation do premise and conclusion have in argument?</i><br>👉 በመነሻ ሃሳብ (Premise) እና በማጠቃለያ (Conclusion) መካከል ያለው ግንኙነት ምንድን ነው?<br>• <i>What is a fallacy? What makes an argument fallacious?</i><br>👉 የሃሳብ ስህተት/ስህተት አቀራረብ (Fallacy) ምንድን ነው?<br><br><hr><br><b><font color='#1565C0'>Lesson 5: Importance of Learning Philosophy</font></b><br><br><b>Overview & Socrates' Quote ፡</b><br>• Philosophy is a rational and critical enterprise that draws on analysis, comparison, and evaluation to address basic human issues.<br>• Socrates famously stated: <b><i>\"The unexamined life is not worth living\"</i></b>. Philosophy provides students with tools to critically examine their own lives and the world.<br>👉 ታዋቂው ፊሎሶፈር ሶክራተስ <b><i>\"ያልተመረመረ ህይወት ዋጋ የለውም\"</i></b> ብሏል። ፊሎሶፊ የራሳችንን ህይወትና ዓለምን በሂስና በትንተና እንድንመረምር ይረዳናል።<br><br><b>Psychological Needs (Maintenance vs. Actualizing Needs):</b><br>• <b>Maintenance Needs:</b> Physical and psychological needs required to maintain ourselves (e.g., food, shelter, security, social interaction).<br>👉 <b>የመኖሪያ/የህልውና ፍላጎቶች፦</b> ህይወትን ለማቆየት የሚያስፈልጉ እንደ ምግብ፣ መጠለያ፣ ደህንነት የመሳሰሉት።<br>• <b>Actualizing Needs:</b> Self-fulfillment, creativity, self-expression, and realizing one's full potential. Philosophy promotes the ideal of self-actualization.<br>👉 <b>ራስን የማደራጀት/የማሳካት ፍላጎቶች፦</b> ራስን መግለጽ፣ የራስን እውነተኛ እቅም ማውጣትና ስኬት ላይ መድረስ። ፊሎሶፊ ለዚህ ትልቅ አስተዋፅዖ ያደርጋል።<br><br><b>Primary Benefits of Studying Philosophy / የፊሎሶፊ ዋና ጥቅሞች፡</b><br><br>1. <b>Intellectual and Behavioral Independence:</b><br>• Ability to develop one's own opinions and systematic worldview. Helps us integrate experiences, thoughts, and feelings to become intellectually independent.<br>👉 በሃሳብና በባህሪ ነፃ መሆን፤ የራሳችንን አመለካከትና የአለም እይታ በራሳችን ምክንያታዊነት እንድንገነባ ይረዳናል።<br><br>2. <b>Reflective Self-Awareness:</b><br>• Intensifies self-awareness by inviting us to critically examine the intellectual grounds of our lives.<br>👉 ራስን በጥልቀት ማወቅና መመርመር።<br><br>3. <b>Flexibility, Tolerance, and Open-Mindedness:</b><br>• Helps us realize that no single viewpoint is necessarily absolute and that the value of attitudes is contextual. We become more tolerant and sympathetic to clashing views.<br>👉 ክፍት አእምሮ ያለው መሆን፣ ሌሎችን መታገስና የሰዎችን የተለያየ ሃሳብ ማስተናገድ።<br><br>4. <b>Creative and Critical Thinking:</b><br>• Refines powers of analysis, abilities to reason, theorize, evaluate, and justify.<br>👉 የትንተና፣ የመሞገት እና በጥልቀት የማሰብ አቅምን ማሳደግ።<br><br>5. <b>Conceptualized Value Systems:</b><br>• Helps formulate feasible evaluations of value in morality, art, and politics to find meaning in life.<br>👉 በህይወት ውስጥ ትርጉም ያለው የእሴት መዋቅር መገንባት።<br><br>6. <b>Dealing with Uncertainty (Bertrand Russell's View):</b><br>• Bertrand Russell noted that the value of philosophy is in its very uncertainty. It frees us from the \"tyranny of custom\", removes arrogant dogmatism, and keeps alive our sense of wonder.<br>👉 በበርትራንድ ረስል እይታ ፊሎሶፊ እርግጠኛ ካልሆኑ ነገሮች ጋር እንድንኖር፣ ከባህል ጭፍን ተፅዕኖ እንድንወጣና የነገሮችን ምስጢር የመመርመር ጉጉታችን እንዳይጠፋ ይረዳል።<br><br><div style='border: 1px solid #D81B60; background-color: #FCE4EC; padding: 12px; border-radius: 8px; margin: 12px 0;'><b><font color='#D81B60'>💡 Exam Hint :</font></b><br>• \"The unexamined life is not worth living\" የማን አባባል ነው ከተባለ፦ <b>Socrates</b>!<br>• \"Applying general moral rules to specific real-world issues like Abortion or Euthanasia\" የትኛው ኤቲክስ ነው ከተባለ፦ <b>Applied Ethics</b>!<br>• \"Value of philosophy is in its uncertainty\" ያለዉ ማን ነው ከተባለ፦ <b>Bertrand Russell</b>!</div><br><hr><br><b><font color='#00796B'>Exam-Style Questions</font></b><br><br><b>1. A study that applies general ethical principles to specific moral issues such as Abortion or Euthanasia is known as:</b><br>A) Normative Ethics<br>B) Meta-ethics<br>C) Applied Ethics<br>D) Aesthetics<br><b>Answer: C</b><br><i>Explanation: Applied Ethics specifically takes moral principles and applies them to specific real-world practical controversies like abortion or euthanasia.</i><br><br><b>2. Which philosopher famously stated that \"The unexamined life is not worth living\"?</b><br>A) Aristotle<br>B) Socrates<br>C) Bertrand Russell<br>D) Plato<br><b>Answer: B</b><br><i>Explanation: Socrates made this statement to emphasize the vital importance of critically examining one's own life and actions.</i><br><br><b>3. According to Bertrand Russell, the primary value of philosophy is to be found in its:</b><br>A) Absolute Certainty<br>B) Practical financial benefits<br>C) Very Uncertainty<br>D) Dogmatic rules<br><b>Answer: C</b><br><i>Explanation: Bertrand Russell argued that philosophy liberates our mind from dogmatism precisely through its uncertainty and by raising possibilities.</i><br><br><hr><br><b><font color='#2E7D32'>🎉 እንኳን ደስላችሁ! Chapter 1ን ሙሉ በሙሉ በጥራት አጠናቀናል። በርቱ፣ በደንብ ከደገማችሁት የLogic ፈተና 100% አይቀርላችሁም! EthioFresh ሁልጊዜ ለስኬታችሁ አብሯችሁ አለ! 🎓✨</font></b>"
‎}
